{
  "kind": "lesson",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "battery-as-push",
  "packId": "lawp.circuits.basics",
  "courseId": "voltage",
  "moduleId": "push",
  "title": "The battery is a push",
  "skillIds": [
    "circuits.voltage",
    "circuits.series.current"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 10,
  "taskRev": 1,
  "description": "Cells add push when you stack them in series. More cells can raise current — they do not ignore resistance or the cap.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## More cells, more push — still a loop\n\nIn this pack one cell is one unit of push. Two cells in series add. Current is still push divided by squeeze: I ≈ cells ÷ ohms. A brighter lamp needs enough current, but the cap is still 2. Extra cells into a tiny resistance is how you overshoot.\n\nThis bites when someone thinks “bigger battery always brighter.” A 3-cell stack through 1 ohm is I = 3, over the cap. Two cells through 2 ohms is I = 1 — bright enough and safe.\n\n![One cell versus two](assets/cells-stack.svg)\n\n```text\nI ≈ cells / ohms\n2 cells, 2 Ω → I = 1   (bright, under 2)\n3 cells, 1 Ω → I = 3   (over the cap)\n```\n\nA common mistake is stacking cells and ignoring the knob. Predict, then pick a pair that lights the lamp without crossing 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "id": "stack-cells",
      "kind": "experiment",
      "engine": "world-v1",
      "promptMd": "Make the lamp brighter without letting current go above 2.",
      "skillIds": [
        "circuits.voltage"
      ],
      "constraintMode": "final",
      "predict": {
        "promptMd": "If you keep ohms at 2 and go from 1 cell to 2 cells, current…",
        "kind": "mcq",
        "choices": [
          {
            "id": "up",
            "md": "Rises (more push, same squeeze)"
          },
          {
            "id": "same",
            "md": "Stays the same because the lamp uses it up",
            "misconceptionId": "current-gets-used-up"
          },
          {
            "id": "always",
            "md": "Will make it brighter at any ohms",
            "misconceptionId": "more-cells-always-brighter"
          }
        ],
        "answer": "up"
      },
      "world": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "id": "battery",
            "type": "battery",
            "props": {
              "cells": 1
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "resistor",
            "type": "resistor",
            "props": {
              "ohms": 2
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "lamp",
            "type": "lamp",
            "props": {
              "brightness": 1,
              "label": "Lamp"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "meter",
            "type": "meter",
            "props": {
              "current": 0.5
            }
          }
        ],
        "connections": [
          {
            "from": "battery",
            "to": "resistor"
          },
          {
            "from": "resistor",
            "to": "lamp"
          },
          {
            "from": "lamp",
            "to": "battery"
          }
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "id": "set-cells",
            "label": "Set cells",
            "target": "battery",
            "op": "set",
            "key": "cells",
            "values": [
              1,
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "set-ohms",
            "label": "Set resistance",
            "target": "resistor",
            "op": "set",
            "key": "ohms",
            "values": [
              1,
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ],
        "rules": [
          {
            "id": "i-from-lookup",
            "when": [],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "meter",
                "key": "current",
                "value": {
                  "op": "div",
                  "a": "battery.cells",
                  "b": "resistor.ohms"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "bright-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "gte",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "dim-from-i",
            "when": [
              {
                "path": "meter.current",
                "op": "lt",
                "value": 1
              }
            ],
            "set": [
              {
                "target": "lamp",
                "key": "brightness",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "view": {
          "kind": "graph",
          "assetMap": {
            "lamp@brightness=0": "assets/lamp-dim.svg",
            "lamp@brightness=1": "assets/lamp-dim.svg",
            "lamp@brightness=2": "assets/lamp-bright.svg",
            "battery": "assets/battery.svg",
            "resistor": "assets/resistor.svg",
            "meter": "assets/meter.svg",
            "voltmeter": "assets/voltmeter.svg",
            "switch@closed=false": "assets/switch-open.svg",
            "switch@closed=true": "assets/switch-closed.svg",
            "fuse": "assets/fuse.svg"
          }
        }
      },
      "goal": {
        "all": [
          {
            "path": "lamp.brightness",
            "op": "eq",
            "value": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        {
          "path": "meter.current",
          "op": "lte",
          "value": 2
        }
      ],
      "explainAfter": {
        "promptMd": "Two cells and 2 ohms gives I = 1: bright and under the cap. Three cells and 1 ohm is I = 3 — more cells, not always a win."
      },
      "misconceptionMap": [
        {
          "when": {
            "path": "meter.current",
            "op": "gt",
            "value": 2
          },
          "misconceptionId": "ignores-current-limit"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Current is cells ÷ ohms. The cap is 2."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "You need I at least 1 for a bright lamp, and I at most 2."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Try 2 cells and 2 ohms. Avoid 3 cells with 1 ohm."
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "Set cells to 2 and ohms to 2, then Check."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "always-brighter",
      "kind": "tf",
      "promptMd": "Three cells will always make this lamp brighter than one cell, even if you drop ohms to 1.",
      "answer": "false",
      "explainMd": "3 ÷ 1 = 3, which blows the cap. More cells are not a free pass.",
      "skillIds": [
        "circuits.voltage"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
